      "description": "Watch Hibernian vs KAA Gent highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 27, 2026. The stage was set for a compelling UEFA Conference League encounter on August 27, 2026, as Hibernian welcomed KAA Gent . Both sides displayed immense energy from the kickoff, signaling their intent to claim a crucial European victory. Tactical Battle and the Opening Goal The match began with a cagey atmosphere as both teams searched for an opening. The intensity manifested early in individual duels, leading to a yellow card for KAA Gent defender Christian Burgess in the 32nd minute. However, the visitors found their rhythm shortly after. In the 39th minute, Tiago Araujo delivered a precise pass to Josue Vergara , who made no mistake in putting the Belgian side ahead. Despite a late first-half caution for Tibe De Vlieger , Gent carried their slim lead into the interval. Hibernian’s Spirited Comeback The second half saw a dramatic shift in momentum as the hosts pushed forward with renewed vigor. Their efforts were rewarded in the 56th minute when Jason Kerr found the back of the net, courtesy of an assist from Jamie McGrath . The equalizer galvanized the home crowd, and Hibernian continued to apply pressure. The turnaround was completed in the 77th minute; Josh Mulligan set up Felix Passlack , who fired his team into a 2-1 lead, seemingly putting the Scottish side in control of the tie. Late Drama and a Cruel Twist Just as Hibernian looked set to secure the win, the game took a chaotic turn in the closing stages. KAA Gent fought back, and in the 84th minute, Christian Burgess turned goalscorer, heading home from a Laszlo Benes delivery to level the scores at 2-2. Disater struck for the hosts in stoppage time when Jordan Obita inadvertently sent the ball into his own net in the 91st minute. To compound the misery, Miguel Chaiwa received his second yellow card and was sent off in the 93rd minute, leaving Hibernian empty-handed after a rollercoaster night."
